\_codedecl \_turtle_loaded {Turtle graphics for OpTeX <2026-08-20>}

\_namespace{turtle}

\_doc
This package provides the basic state and movement primitives for Logo-like
Turtle graphics. The turtle starts at the current TeX position and points
upward. Distances are measured in TeX points.
\_cod

\_def\.vecx#1{\_ea\.vecxA#1}
\_def\.vecxA(#1 #2){#1}
\_def\.vecy#1{\_ea\.vecyA#1}
\_def\.vecyA(#1 #2){#2}
\_def\.scalev#1#2{(\expr{#1 * \.vecx#2} \expr{#1 * \.vecy#2})}
\_def\.sumv#1#2{(\expr{\.vecx#1 + \.vecx#2} \expr{\.vecy#1 + \.vecy#2})}

\_newifi\_ifturtle_pendown
\_def\.turtlepenup{\_turtle_pendownfalse}
\_def\.turtlependown{\_turtle_pendowntrue}
\_def\.turtlepensize#1{\_edef\.pensizevalue{#1}}
\_doc
The drawing backend is isolated in the internal drawsegment macro. It receives
five arguments: start x, start y, end x, end y, and pen width. The default
backend uses the ordinary OpTeX pdfliteral whatsit. A replacement backend
can be installed with turtlebackend followed by its macro name.
\_cod

\_def\.drawsegment#1#2#3#4#5{%
   \_pdfliteral{q 1 J #5 w #1 #2 m #3 #4 l S Q}}
\_def\.turtlebackend#1{\_let\.drawsegment=#1}

\_doc
The movement commands are available inside begturtle and use a
space-delimited argument. For example, write forward 40 followed by a space.
The short names forward, backward, right, left, penup, pendown, pensize,
repeat, and backend are local to the begturtle scope.
\_cod

\_def\.turtleforward#1 {%
   \_let\.startpos\.pos
   \_edef\.displacement{\.scalev{#1}{(\_sin{\.angle} \_cos{\.angle})}}%
   \_edef\.pos{\.sumv\.pos\.displacement}%
   \_ifturtle_pendown
      \.drawsegment
         {\expr{\.vecx\.startpos}}
         {\expr{\.vecy\.startpos}}
         {\expr{\.vecx\.pos}}
         {\expr{\.vecy\.pos}}
         {\.pensizevalue}%
   \_fi
}

\_def\.turtlebackward#1 {\.turtleforward -#1 }
\_def\.turtleright#1 {%
   \_edef\.angle{\expr{\.angle + #1}}}
\_def\.turtleleft#1 {\.turtleright -#1 }
\_def\.turtlerepeat#1 #2{\_fornum 1..#1 \_do{#2}}

\_doc
The begturtle and endturtle commands open and close a local turtle scope.
Inside the scope, short names are available for the turtle primitives. The
Each begturtle starts at position (0,0), points upward, and resets the pen to
down with width 1. The original meanings of the short names are restored by
endturtle.
\_cod

\_def\.begturtle{\_begingroup
   \_def\.pos{(0.000 0.000)}
   \_def\.angle{0}
   \_turtle_pendowntrue
   \.turtlepensize{1}
   \_let\forward\.turtleforward
   \_let\backward\.turtlebackward
   \_let\right\.turtleright
   \_let\left\.turtleleft
   \_let\penup\.turtlepenup
   \_let\pendown\.turtlependown
   \_let\pensize\.turtlepensize
   \_let\backend\.turtlebackend
   \_let\repeat\.turtlerepeat}
\_def\.endturtle{\_endgroup}

\_nspublic \begturtle \endturtle ;

\_endnamespace
\_endcode

\_doc
Higher-level drawings belong in user documents or separate example files.
For example:
\begtt
\load[turtle]
\begturtle
\def\square#1 {\repeat 4 {\forward #1 \right 90 }}
\square 60
\endturtle
\endtt
\_cod
\endinput
